.TH TINEPLAYER 1 "2026-08-01" "TinePlayer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tineplayer \- play a video with two audio tracks on two output devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tineplayer
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TinePlayer
plays one video with two soundtracks at once, sending each to a different
output device, so that two people can watch the same screen together and each
hear it their own way. One hears the film in English through the television
while the other hears it in Spanish through headphones, and the two stay in
sync because it is one pipeline decoding one file.
.PP
The same split carries audio description: someone who needs the narrated
version hears it on headphones while everyone else hears the ordinary
soundtrack.
.PP
Run with no arguments to choose everything from the menu: the video, the two
output devices, the audio track for each, and the subtitles. Pass a
.I FILE
to open it directly. A file may be a path or a URL, including
.BR http:// " and " smb:// .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-primary " TRACK"
Audio for the primary output. A track number as
.B \-\-list\-tracks
prints them, a language code such as
.BR en ,
.B ad
for described audio, or
.B en:ad
for both. Use
.B 0
for no audio on that output.
.TP
.BI \-\-secondary " TRACK"
Audio for the secondary output, in the same forms.
.TP
.BI \-\-subtitle " SUBTITLE"
Subtitles to show: a track number, a language code, the name of a subtitle
file beside the video, or a preference name.
.B 0
for none.
.TP
.B \-\-play
Start playing straight away, without the menu, using the tracks remembered for
that video or your language preferences. Needs a
.I FILE
and a primary output device already set.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-tracks
Print the file's audio tracks and subtitles with their numbers, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-devices
Print this machine's audio output device names, one per line, and exit. These
are the names
.I config.yaml
matches against.
.TP
.B \-\-restart
Start from the beginning, ignoring any saved position.
.TP
.B \-\-forget
Forget saved positions and track choices. With a
.IR FILE ,
forgets only that one; with none, forgets them all.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start fullscreen.
.TP
.B \-\-windowed
Start windowed, overriding a remembered fullscreen preference.
.TP
.B \-\-external
Play only the video given, with no file browser and no confirmation on the way
out, exiting when the video ends. For launching from another application.
.TP
.B \-\-kodi
Launched by Kodi: keep the resume position in step with Kodi's library.
Implies
.BR \-\-external .
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of these options.
.TP
.B \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tineplayer/config.yaml
Settings: output devices, preferred languages, subtitle appearance, interface
scale. A file that cannot be parsed is copied aside rather than overwritten,
and TinePlayer starts on defaults and says so.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tineplayer/
Saved playback positions and per-video track choices.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation, including how to hand playback over from Kodi, at
.UR https://github.com/scottarius/TinePlayer
.UE .
